From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lee Kage <magic-smoke@tinytapeout.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:31:12 +0000
Subject: ulinux_asic: execute-in-place kernel from SPI flash (make
 xip)

Add CONFIG_NOMMU_XIP_KERNEL: a no-MMU RISC-V kernel whose text, rodata
and built-in initramfs run from the memory-mapped SPI flash at
0x20200000, with data/bss in PSRAM. head.S copies the data section from
flash itself, so the XIP bootloader only jumps to the flash and no longer
needs IMAGE_SIZE. Jump labels, preempt-dynamic keys and alternatives are
disabled because they patch kernel text.

The bootloader also gets WORD_COPY=1 for the normal (copying) boot: one
32-bit flash read and PSRAM write per word instead of per byte.

On ttsky25a silicon: reset to shell 209 s (byte copy) / 152 s (word copy)
/ 128 s (XIP); MemTotal 13968 -> 15768 KB. Execution speed unchanged.

Targets: make xip (xip/Image + xip/bootloader.bin), make xip-sim (QEMU pflash).

Rebased on upstream cc05de6, whose bootloader already copies by words: the
XIP patch no longer adds its own WORD_COPY option.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
