 That's it! Your system is now ready to use.
 
+
+## Execute-in-place (XIP) kernel
+
+`make xip` (after `make all`) builds `xip/Image`, a kernel whose text, rodata and built-in
+initramfs run directly from the SPI flash; only data and BSS (about 450 KB) live in PSRAM, and
+the kernel copies its data section itself. `xip/bootloader.bin` just jumps to the flash.
+Flash it as: `xip/bootloader.bin` @0x100000, `kianv.dtb` @0x180000, `xip/Image` @0x200000
+(the Image is linked for 0x20200000 and works nowhere else). `make xip-sim` boots it in QEMU
+from a pflash.
+
+Measured on ttsky25a silicon (30 MHz), same rootfs:
+
+| | old byte-copy bootloader | default bootloader (8 words per iteration) | XIP |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| bootloader copy | 79 s | 8 s | none |
+| reset to `/ # ` | 209 s | about 138 s | 128 s |
+| MemTotal / MemFree after boot | 13968 / 10396 KB | same | 15768 / 12196 KB |
+
+Kernel and userspace speed are unchanged (flash and PSRAM go through the same quad-SPI
+controller with the same timing; there is no cache). Kernel patch:
+`bldroot/board/kianv/rv32ima/patches/linux/0010-riscv-nommu-execute-in-place-kernel.patch`
+(`CONFIG_NOMMU_XIP_KERNEL`, fragment `xip/linux-xip.fragment`).
